-- Test fixture: the two-tenant seed the integration tests run against.
--
-- Extracted with `pg_dump --data-only --column-inserts` from the development database
-- `ptr-clone-postgres-1`, which is where these rows were originally seeded by hand. Committing
-- them is the point: until now the 9 RLS tests, the auth tests and the refresh-rotation tests
-- all depended on one developer's local container, so CI could not run them at all and a lost
-- volume would have taken the fixture with it.
--
-- Two tenants - `acme-trading` and `beta-trading` - each with one room, because the property
-- under test is that neither can see the other. A single-tenant fixture cannot fail the test it
-- exists for.
--
-- Deliberately NOT included:
--   * `_sqlx_migrations` - the ledger is built by running migrations, never by loading it.
--   * `refresh_tokens`   - live credentials, even test ones, do not belong in a committed file;
--                          `refresh_rotation.rs` issues its own.
--   * `audit_log`        - a record of the fixture's own creation. Noise.
--
-- ## Statement order is load-bearing
--
-- The tables are emitted in foreign-key dependency order, one `pg_dump -t` per table, rather
-- than in pg_dump's default alphabetical order. `SET CONSTRAINTS ALL DEFERRED` is not an option
-- here: **none of this schema's 30 foreign keys is DEFERRABLE**, so deferral silently does
-- nothing and the load fails on `rooms_owner_fk` instead.
--
-- `users` and `rooms` genuinely reference each other (`rooms.owner_id` and
-- `users.guest_created_in_room_id`). Users come first, which works because no seeded user is a
-- guest - checked when this file was generated, and asserted at the end of it.
--
-- Load AFTER migrations, as the owner:
--   psql "$MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f services/api/fixtures/seed.sql

BEGIN;

-- A second load would violate a primary key part way through and leave the fixture half
-- applied. Refuse up front instead, naming the reason.
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM public.enterprises) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'this database already has tenants; seed.sql expects a freshly migrated one';
  END IF;
END
$$;

